# EMDR — letter-rise on big marketing titles

Do **not** skip this. When the user says “scroll animation like the other sections” for **big titles**, they mean **letter-rise**, not GSAP `fe-animate`.

## Always

Marketing section **H2** (and equivalent display titles: pricing, blog, FAQ, stories, footer CTA, `SessionLoopKit`, `SessionTopicsGrid`, `SessionModesPair`, `HomePauseCta`, `HomeMemorySets`): `LetterRevealHeading` from `app/components/frontend/LetterRevealHeading.tsx`.

Letters rise from below (`fe-letter-rise` / `fe-letter-fade`). That component already replays when the heading is fully off-screen, then scrolled in again.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
<p className="fe-section-kicker fe-animate">Your language</p>
<LetterRevealHeading className="fe-section-title">
  A calm session in many languages.
</LetterRevealHeading>

// ❌ BAD — GSAP block fade is not the title motion
<h2 className="fe-section-title fe-animate">A calm session in many languages.</h2>
```

## Never for those titles

- `.fe-animate` on the heading or wrapping `.fe-section-head`
- `gsap.from` / `fromTo` `y` + `opacity` as a stand-in for letter-rise
- “Fix replay” by changing `useLandingMotion` section fades — leave `.fe-animate` for **kicker / body / cards** only
- Inventing a new title tween

`.fe-animate` + ScrollTrigger stays on small copy and cards (`toggleActions: "play none none none"`).

## Exceptions (do not letter-rise)

| Surface | Motion |
|---|---|
| Home hero **H1** | `.fe-split-word` on load |
| Session path **intro** H2 | Attio ink→muted inline fade — not `LetterRevealHeading` |
| Session path **stage / pair / finale** leads | `LetterRevealHeading` (`eager` on sticky leads) |
| `/app`, `/admin`, legal/long-form | Source Sans, no letter-rise |

